orm_id":"nd8e22e5830cb74a7","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Reduce the description to at most 8000 characters, usually by splitting independent work into coherent child tickets.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Record, in the plan, the expected savings magnitude derived from the prior ropeable-hydrated-siskin overhead evidence (~5% of the ~5-6m Ubuntu default-suite step, i.e. tens of seconds across the two changed cells) so the runner-seconds-freed target and the survey/contract/umbrella machinery can be weighed against it.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["The predecessor ticket ropeable-hydrated-siskin (f3d4) recorded: 'an independent measurement of coverage.py overhead on this suite came in at +5.1% (61.5s -> 64.7s at -n 3 on a subset)' and 'the honest expectation is ~0.8 min off an ~18.6m macOS job, not a large win.'","docs/coverage.md sizes the ubuntu default-suite steps at '~5-6m for the same tests on ubuntu' — so a ~5% coverage overhead on the TWO cells being changed is on the order of tens of seconds, not minutes.","The plan mounts a new workflow contract with two defect-seeded RED proofs, a three-project (Django/NumPy/SciPy) consensus survey with a stop-gate, and an open umbrella (inedible-subsimious-brahmancow) for post-merge delta tracking.","The plan already shows optimization-cost awareness ('must label a one-run comparison as noisy', 'must not call summed parallel time critical-path wall time'), which defuses over-claiming but does not state the expected savings size."],"finding":"The change is a runner-cost optimization whose expected absolute savings are small by the project's own prior evidence, yet the plan does not state that magnitude up front against the cost of the machinery it introduces.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff50b2ea774d631da","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Context' and 'Plan' (the A-B-B-A-A-B experiment + survey + umbrella tracking); AC lines on local_delta and runner-seconds freed.","norm_id":"n154f4b0676a73e70","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer or operator weighing whether the survey + contract + umbrella machinery is proportionate to the benefit has no up-front magnitude estimate and must reconstruct it from the linked f3d4 comments.","The post-merge report records 'runner-seconds freed' but a reader cannot tell whether the result met or missed a prior expectation because none was stated."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the edit-target wording: name the exact workflow string being conditioned (`--cov=rebar --cov-report=term-missing:skip-covered`) and state that branch coverage and fail_under come from pyproject.toml ([tool.coverage.run] branch=true, [tool.coverage.report] fail_under=70) and activate wherever --cov is passed — not from a workflow flag.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.425,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Plan: 'the non-empty coverage flag string in the truthy and-slot'","Plan: 'both state that Ubuntu Python 3.13 alone collects branch coverage and enforces fail-under'",".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml:751 passes `--cov=rebar --cov-report=term-missing:skip-covered` (no --cov-branch)","pyproject.toml:573 `branch = true`; pyproject.toml:590 `fail_under = 70`","search for `--cov-branch` in the workflow returned (no matches)"],"finding":"The plan names the Ubuntu-3.13 edit target as toggling 'branch coverage' and 'fail-under', but those are configured in pyproject.toml ([tool.coverage.run] branch = true; [tool.coverage.report] fail_under = 70), not by any workflow flag. The workflow's actual coverage flags are `--cov=rebar --cov-report=term-missing:skip-covered` — there is no --cov-branch or --cov-fail-under in _build-and-test.yml.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f974b4c9953b26242","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan 'Encode the condition...' / 'Update the coverage rationale comment...' bullets and ACs 'Ubuntu Python 3.13 collects branch coverage' / 'enforces the unchanged fail-under threshold'","norm_id":"nd3360b941cd5ba20","priority":0.275,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Author edits the workflow expecting a --cov-branch/--cov-fail-under flag to add/move and finds none","The docs/comment text asserts the workflow 'enables branch coverage' when the workflow only passes --cov and pyproject supplies branch/floor"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_pl